# Qwen3-Embedding-8B Q6_K served by the installed stable llama.cpp build.
# Pooling is 'last': Qwen3-Embedding is a causal LM whose sentence vector is the
# final-token hidden state. Using mean/cls here silently degrades recall.
# UBATCH must be >= the longest single chunk, because a pooled sequence cannot be
# split across micro-batches; the RAG ingester caps chunks well under this.
SIDECAR_PORT=8081
SIDECAR_ALIAS=qwen3-embedding-8b
SIDECAR_MODEL=/home/typhoon/git/frankenstein-llm/models/embedding/Qwen3-Embedding-8B-Q6_K.gguf
SIDECAR_DEVICE=ROCm0,ROCm1,ROCm2
SIDECAR_NGL=all
SIDECAR_CTX=4096
SIDECAR_BATCH=4096
SIDECAR_UBATCH=4096
# Placement: one card. 3,6,2 was the pre-2026-09-06 catalog default and gave the
# throttling V620 the majority of the layers of a model that fits on a single
# 6900 XT. llama-models.ini stopped using it in f2576ac; this file was not
# updated with it. Layer split is pipelined, so every token crossed two extra
# devices for no capacity reason. Measured on kernel 7.2.3-273-tkg-eevdf-llvm,
# pp512/tg128, r=3, native llama-bench: 34.63 -> 65.32 tok/s decode (+88.7%),
# 1234.53 -> 1430.10 tok/s prefill (+15.8%). Embeddings never decode, so the
# prefill figure is the one that describes this service.
SIDECAR_EXTRA_ARGS=--embedding --pooling last --embd-normalize 2 --flash-attn on --tensor-split 1,0,0
